# {{ name }}/playground

Scratch space for trying `{{ name }}` against throwaway facts before
committing a real `examples/` entry. Nothing here is load-bearing --
`ggen sync run --dry-run` here should always be safe to run repeatedly.

Suggested flow:
1. Copy a real fact shape into `scratch.ttl` (start from this pack's own
   `qualification/` fixtures if any exist yet, or a minimal individual of
   whatever class `ontology.ttl` declares first).
2. `ggen sync run --dry-run --ontology scratch.ttl` from this directory
   (or point at the pack's real `ggen.toml` if one exists) and read the
   real rendered output before deciding it's example-worthy.
3. Promote what actually works to `../examples/`, not what looks plausible.

